WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.920
 If you are not a
nudist, style is for you.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:09.540
I've been in the fashion and
styling business for 20 years.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.700
Most people know me
from "Queer Eye."

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.410
I've probably helped
literally thousands of people

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:16.110
find their personal
style and find

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:18.690
a look that makes them
feel good about themselves.

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:20.220
I want you to look
in your closet

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.680
and decide, who do I want to be?

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.600
What do I want to feel?

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.305
I just want you
to make an effort.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.820
This class is different from
anything I've ever done before.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:35.060
I will comprehensively
break down what style is

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:36.830
and how the principles work.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:41.000
American men, plaid is not
your only option for a print.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.410
Move on.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:44.030
It is absolutely
possible for you

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:46.310
to have great style
on any budget.

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:49.680
The key is a capsule wardrobe.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:50.590
This is your base.

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:52.610
This is your foundation.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:57.980
All of these items could be worn
time after time and reimagined.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:01.910
I devoted my life to style
because it affected me so

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:03.200
greatly as a child.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:07.250
I so desperately wanted to
show who I really was inside,

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:10.460
but I couldn't because of
my culture and my faith.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:13.460
When I was seven, I went
to my granddad's factory.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:14.960
He made denim.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.060
And for the first
time, I understood

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:19.370
where clothes came from,
how they were created,

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:21.110
and how they could make me feel.

00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:23.300
And so I started to
experiment with clothes,

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.390
and my clothes gave me a
window into the world that I

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:28.220
could only have dreamt of.

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:29.960
I want you to
really start to see

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:32.030
your closet as a
vehicle to getting

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:33.510
what you want from your life.

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.960
I want you to really
feel something

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:37.930
when you get dressed
in the morning.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:40.490
Every day, know that
you've made an effort.

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:42.582
Be the reason that you're happy.

00:01:42.582 --> 00:01:45.820
I'm Tan France, and
this is my MasterClass.

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:48.270
[MUSIC PLAYING]

